            <ArticleTitle>Effect of off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting on morbidity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1021-2, A10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three hundred three patients who underwent off-pump coronary bypass were compared with 483 patients who underwent standard on-pump coronary bypass. There was a significant reduction in intraoperative blood transfusion requirements, as well as a significant reduction in the incidence of neurologic, renal, and prolonged ventilatory complications in the off-pump group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
